    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493296169/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """remains pleasant, and he is improved. We walked over to the Lawsons to see his portraits of Lina and myself, which – from the drawing of the faces – we liked very much. This was a great comfort to dear little Mrs. Kerr-Lawson who had been trembling with anxiety all day. 
Saturday June 11. 1898.
Bernhard’s dealer from Rome (Cesare Magni, by name!) came bringing a lovely Rembrandt he bought, and some Japanese bronzes. Later came Torrini with a Sienese portrait, which Bernhard also bought. The Rosses came to tea – also an American named Rush and his wife and a friend. """^^xsd:string ;
